    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d164">

                <pb facs="0497" n="460" sameAs="frus:frus1951-54Iran/pg460"/>

                <head>164. Telegram From the Department of State to the Embassy in Iran<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d164-f1"/></head>
                <dateline><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                        when="1953-02-27T17:43:00-05:00">February 27, 1953, 5:43
                    p.m</date>.</dateline>
                <p>2238. In view Shah’s apparent desire leave Iran and Mosadeq’s position that Shah
                    should leave, Department sees little which could usefully be done to prevent
                    Shah’s departure. We are currently assessing significance this crisis and
                    developments likely flow from Shah’s departure, and would appreciate any
                    comments you may have in amplification urtel 3397<anchor n="2" xml:id="d164-f2"
                    /> rpt London 1103. Department will attempt minimize to press significance
                    Shah’s departure Iran but there is every likelihood press will take line that
                    Shah has fled Iran and his case is similar to Farouk’s.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>Dulles</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
